 ## Overview
-Direction-dependent Morton Order Mapping is a remapping function that converts a standard Octree Morton code into a sorting key aligned with the near-to-far rendering order for a specific ray direction. It solves the problem of correct occlusion culling and blending order in sparse voxel rasterization by ensuring that voxels are processed from closest to furthest relative to the camera, regardless of the viewing angle [S1]. Unlike [Point Location](2076-point-location.md) which determines spatial containment, or [Fast Projection for Octree Nodes](2178-fast-projection-for-octree-nodes.md) which estimates bounding volumes, this method specifically addresses the topological sorting requirement for volume rendering by adapting the Morton space-filling curve to the ray's sign vector [S1].
