 ## Background
-The method originates from the work on Sparse Voxels Rasterization for real-time high-fidelity Radiance Field rendering [S1]. It addresses the limitation of standard Morton ordering, which assumes a fixed viewing direction (typically $+,+,+$), by generalizing the space-filling curve permutation to eight possible octants defined by ray direction signs. The correctness of the ordering is proven by induction on the Octree level, showing that the base case ($\ell=1$) aligns with the ray direction and that subdivision preserves this order [S1].
